  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainably improve the health of the Senegalese populations through health systems strengthening - Senegal (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Senegal, RSSH, Ministry of Health and Social Action of the Republic of Senegal (MSAS)This program has the following goals: Sustainably improve Senegalese health. The objectives of this program are: Appropriately treat at least 60 percent of people with STIs who consult health centers by 2017..  By 2017, offer antiretrovirals to at least 90 percent of pregnant women who are newly tested HIV-positive to reduce HIV transmission to the child..  Diagnose at least 75 percent of expected TB cases (all forms)..  HSS O-1: Achieve a 75 percent attendance rate for antenatal consultations.  Protect 80 percent of pregnant women using IPT with sulfadoxine pyrimethamine in accordance with national guidelines..  Reduce blood transmission of HIV, HCV and HCB to zero throughout the entire region..  Successfully treat at least 90 percent of new diagnosed TB cases.&#xa0;.  Treat 100 percent of malaria cases in pregnant women seen in health facilities in accordance with national guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
